ps://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/authentication/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/authentication/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Commands</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Commands&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;List of the available commands and their description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;file&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The runbook file location&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;!!! example &#34;Example&#34;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;`automatiqal --file path...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/commands/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Examples</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Examples&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;For runbook examples please check:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Informatiqal/automatiqal-cli/tree/main/runbook-examples&#34;&gt;Automatiqal CLI Tests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;[Auto...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/examples/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Initial checks</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Initial checks&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Automatiqal&lt;/code&gt; will perform few initial checks &lt;strong&gt;before start running&lt;/strong&gt; the tasks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If any of these checks fails then the process will exit ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/initial-checks/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Installation</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Install&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Installation is quite simple:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install -g automatiqal-cli&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once the installation is complete just run:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;automatiqal --help&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To verify that...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/install/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Multiple environments</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Multiple environments&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The default behavior of the runbook is &#34;one runbook one environment&#34;. Usually this is more than enough but there are cases where the...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/multiple-environments/</guid> </item> <item> <title>onError block</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;OnError&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each task can have a &lt;code&gt;try ... catch&lt;/code&gt; workflow defined.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;onError&lt;/code&gt; block is just a list of tasks to be performed if &lt;code&gt;Automatiqal&lt;/code&gt; encounter an ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/on-error-block/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Output</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Outputs&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two output related flags are available:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Output&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When this flag is used the raw output will be saved as json format in the provided file name:...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/output/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Runbook structure</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Runbook structure&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The runbook have 3 main parts:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#header&#34;&gt;Header&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#environment&#34;&gt;Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#tasks&#34;&gt;Tasks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Header&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;```yamlname: Sample run...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/runbook-structure/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Schema</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Schema&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Great little addition is the availability of &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Informatiqal/automatiqal-cli-schema&#34;&gt;YAML schema&lt;/a&gt;. The schema greatly helps when w...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/schema/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Conditions</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Conditions&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apart from &lt;code&gt;skip&lt;/code&gt; property, which have to be set explicitly, tasks can be skipped based on condition. &lt;code&gt;when&lt;/code&gt; condition can be set for tasks and...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/conditions/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Filter/source</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Filter/source&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;When working with existing entities in QMC (apps, streams, reload tasks, virtual proxies etc.) we can use &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt; task property to...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/filter-source/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Import</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Import&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tasks can also be defined in external files and imported into the current runbook. The basic syntax is:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;```yaml- task: ... - import: path\to...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/import/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/import/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/import/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Loop</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Loops&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;!!! note &#34;&#34;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;`Automatiqal v0.4+`&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Task can be executed multiple times by using &lt;code&gt;loop&lt;/code&gt; property. For example if the task is to create 3 tags then...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/loop/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/loop/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/loop/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Operations list</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Operations list&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;List of available operations. The aim is to cover as many Qlik Repo API endpoints as possible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;!!! note&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;This list needs updating. Mo...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/operations-list/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/operations-list/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/operations-list/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Task options</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Task options&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;In contrast with the task details, options are common for all &lt;a href=&#34;./operations-list.md&#34;&gt;operations&lt;/a&gt;. Some of them might not make sense for speci...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/options/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/options/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/options/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Task block</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Task&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each task can be &#34;split&#34; into two sections - meta and details&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Meta&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;```yaml- name: Create custom property description: create new custom prope...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-block/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-block/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-block/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Concurrency and parallel</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Concurrency and parallel options&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Few concurrency task options are available when operation is performed on multiple entities (apps, streams etc.).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Par...&lt;/h2&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-concurrency/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-concurrency/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/task-details/task-concurrency/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Variables</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Variables&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are two type of variables that can be setup:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#static&#34;&gt;Static&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#runtime&#34;&gt;Runtime&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Static&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To define static variable just wra...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/variables/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2025 19:19:14 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://informatiqal.com/feed_rss_created.xml">Informatiqal</source><comments>https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/variables/null</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://informatiqal.com/automatiqal/cli/variables/</guid> </item> </channel></rss>